=== crlf, width 80, default
Changelog

All notable changes are documented here.

[Unreleased]

Added

• A --dry-run flag that shows what would change without touching a file.
• Support for ~/.config/frobnicate/frobnicate.toml, read before the project's
  own file.

Fixed

• A crash when a file name contained a combining character, such as é.
• The progress bar overwrote the last line of the output on narrow terminals; it
  now stays within the terminal width.

[2.1.0] - 2026-09-12

Changed

• Jobs default to the number of CPU cores, up to 8.
• Error messages name the file first, then the reason.

Deprecated

• --legacy-output, which will go away in 3.0. Use --format=plain.

[2.0.0] - 2026-05-02

Removed

• The --old-syntax flag and the .frobrc file.

Changed

• Breaking: the exit code for partial failure is 1, no longer 3.
